# Keeps the Docker build context small — this directory is the build context for every
# service whose docker-compose.yml entry uses "context: ../backend" (audit-service,
# auth-service_1, trip-service_2, gps-service_2, incident-service_3, notification-service_5).
# None of this is needed: each Dockerfile does a fresh `mvn clean package` from pom.xml + src,
# so shipping old target/ jars (each ~70-80MB) and debug logs to the daemon just slows every
# build and wastes memory — worth avoiding on a resource-constrained deploy VM.
**/target/
**/*.class
**/build-output*.txt
**/build-task*.txt
**/build-rabbit*.txt
**/build-gps*.txt
**/hs_err_pid*.log
**/replay_pid*.log
**/*.log
.git/
.idea/
**/*.iml
